Give configure's compiler probe a variadic parameter list, for gcc 15.

WHY: gmp's own "is this compiler usable" test is pre-C23 C, and gcc 15 defaults
to gnu23. config.log from the run:

    configure:6585: gcc -O2 -pedantic  conftest.c >&5
    conftest.c:12:48: error: too many arguments to function 'g';
                      expected 0, have 6
    conftest.c:7:6: note: declared here
        7 | void g(){}

The probe declares `void g(){}` and calls it with six arguments. In C17 an
empty parameter list means UNSPECIFIED parameters and the call is legal; in C23
it means `(void)`. All four attempts fail identically -- gcc and cc, ABI=64 and
ABI=32 -- and configure then reports "could not find a working compiler", which
reads as a broken toolchain and is a language change.

THIS IS THE LFS FIX, NOT AN INVENTED ONE. LFS 13.0 chapter 8 carries the same
edit and names the reason: "First, make an adjustment for compatibility with
gcc-15 and later."

    sed -i '/long long t1;/,+1s/()/(...)/' configure

WHY A PATCH RATHER THAN THAT sed. ROADMAP.md's first rule makes the recipe the
unit and says a reader of one recipe should see everything strange about that
package. Four packages in this set modify source -- glib, graphite2 and wlroots
twice -- and every one does it as a patch, because `apply_patches` records them
in PLAN.txt by name and fails the build if one no longer applies. A sed that
matches nothing succeeds silently and ships an unmodified file. Both hunks are
generated by `diff -u` rather than written by hand, after a hand-written hunk
for wlroots was rejected as malformed.

WHY NOT CC="gcc -std=gnu17". That was the first fix here and it is broader than
the fault: it pins a whole package to a five-year-old language revision to
correct one construct, and gmp builds its own optimisation and ABI flag lists
that a CC override can disturb -- which matters for the one package whose
assembly selection this project already pins a triplet to control.

BOTH OCCURRENCES ARE PATCHED. The probe appears twice, at configure:6570 and
configure:8189, and only fixing the first leaves the second to fail later.

--- a/configure
+++ b/configure
@@ -6568,7 +6568,7 @@
 
 #if defined (__GNUC__) && ! defined (__cplusplus)
 typedef unsigned long long t1;typedef t1*t2;
-void g(){}
+void g(...){}
 void h(){}
 static __inline__ t1 e(t2 rp,t2 up,int n,t1 v0)
 {t1 c,x,r;int i;if(v0){c=1;for(i=1;i<n;i++){x=up[i];r=x+1;rp[i]=r;}}return c;}
@@ -8187,7 +8187,7 @@
 
 #if defined (__GNUC__) && ! defined (__cplusplus)
 typedef unsigned long long t1;typedef t1*t2;
-void g(){}
+void g(...){}
 void h(){}
 static __inline__ t1 e(t2 rp,t2 up,int n,t1 v0)
 {t1 c,x,r;int i;if(v0){c=1;for(i=1;i<n;i++){x=up[i];r=x+1;rp[i]=r;}}return c;}
